    {
      "id": "upperbidiagonalization-blocked-helper",
      "name": "upperbidiagonalization_blocked_helper",
      "category": "UpperBidiagonalization",
      "signature": "upperbidiagonalization_blocked_helper(Target, A, Diagonal, Upper Diagonal, Bs, X, Y)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UpperBidiagonalization*"
        },
        {
          "name": "A",
          "type": "MatrixType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Diagonal",
          "type": "MatrixType::RealScalar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Upper Diagonal",
          "type": "MatrixType::RealScalar*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Bs",
          "type": "Index"
        },
        {
          "name": "X",
          "type": "Ref<Matrix<MatrixType::Scalar,Dynamic,Dynamic,traits<MatrixType>::Flags& RowMajorBit>>"
        },
        {
          "name": "Y",
          "type": "Ref<Matrix<MatrixType::Scalar,Dynamic,Dynamic,traits<MatrixType>::Flags& RowMajorBit>>"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<MatrixType> void",
      "docs": "\\internal\nHelper routine for the block reduction to upper bidiagonal form.\nLet's partition the matrix A:\n| A00 A01 |\nA = |         |\n| A10 A11 |\nThis function reduces to bidiagonal form the left \\c rows x \\a blockSize vertical panel [A00/A10]\nand the \\a blockSize x \\c cols horizontal panel [A00 A01] of the matrix \\a A. The bottom-right block A11\nis updated using matrix-matrix products:\nA22 -= V * Y^T - X * U^T\nwhere V and U contains the left and right Householder vectors. U and V are stored in A10, and A01\nrespectively, and the update matrices X and Y are computed during the reduction."
    },
    {
      "id": "upperbidiagonalization-inplace-blocked",
      "name": "upperbidiagonalization_inplace_blocked",
      "category": "UpperBidiagonalization",
      "signature": "upperbidiagonalization_inplace_blocked(Target, A, Bidiagonal, Max Block Size, Scalar)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UpperBidiagonalization*"
        },
        {
          "name": "A",
          "type": "MatrixType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Bidiagonal",
          "type": "BidiagType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Max Block Size",
          "type": "Index",
          "default": "32"
        },
        {
          "name": "Scalar",
          "type": "MatrixType::",
          "default": "0"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<MatrixType,BidiagType> void",
      "docs": "\\internal\nImplementation of a block-bidiagonal reduction.\nIt is based on the following paper:\nThe Design of a Parallel Dense Linear Algebra Software Library: Reduction to Hessenberg, Tridiagonal, and Bidiagonal Form.\nby Jaeyoung Choi, Jack J. Dongarra, David W. Walker. (1995)\nsection 3.3"
    },
